          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><code>slider</code> = <strong>45</strong>,\n<code>range_slider</code> = <strong>[20, 70]</strong>,\n<code>number</code> = <strong>42</strong></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Reach for a <strong>slider</strong> when the exact figure doesn't matter and you want\npeople to explore a range by feel \u2014 a threshold, an opacity, a year. Use\n<strong>range_slider</strong> when you're picking a <em>window</em> rather than a point, like a\nmin/max filter. Use <strong>number</strong> when the precise value does matter and typing\n<code>42</code> is quicker than dragging to it.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
