            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><code>date</code> = <strong>2026-07-22</strong>, <code>date_range</code> = <strong>(datetime.date(2026, 7, 22), datetime.date(2026, 7, 22))</strong>,\n<code>datetime</code> = <strong>2026-07-22 08:22:05</strong></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Each hands back a real <code>datetime.date</code>/<code>datetime.datetime</code>, not a string,\nso no parsing at your end. Use <strong>date</strong> for a single day, <strong>date_range</strong>\nfor a from/to filter over a dataframe, and <strong>datetime</strong> when the time of\nday matters. All three take <code>start</code>/<code>stop</code> to fence off the allowed range.</span></span>"
