    {
      "id": "TqIu",
      "code_hash": "c416c1a416e545876e63773c48b7b491",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">button clicked <strong>1</strong> times; run_button pressed:\n<strong>True</strong>.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">These are for <em>actions</em> rather than values. A plain <strong>button</strong> carries\nwhatever <code>value</code> you compute in <code>on_click</code> \u2014 above it counts clicks.\n<strong>run_button</strong> is the escape hatch from reactivity: gate an expensive cell\nbehind <code>if not run.value: mo.stop()</code> so it only fires when asked.\n<strong>refresh</strong> re-runs its dependents on a timer, which is what you want for\npolling a file or an API. (There's also <code>mo.ui.microphone</code> for audio and\n<code>mo.ui.file</code>/<code>file_browser</code> next.)</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
