    {
      "id": "xXTn",
      "code_hash": "b353f95e4ff7404bd61da950392f7ed3",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><code>array</code> = <strong>[0, 1, 2]</strong>, <code>dictionary</code> = <strong>{'first': '', 'last': ''}</strong>,\n<code>form</code> = <strong>None</strong>, <code>batch</code> = <strong>{'drink': 'tea', 'temp': 80}</strong></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Use <strong>array</strong> when the <em>number</em> of widgets isn't known ahead of time \u2014\none slider per column of a dataframe, say. Use <strong>dictionary</strong> for the same\nidea with meaningful keys instead of positions. Wrap anything in <strong>form</strong>\nwhen reacting on every keystroke would be wasteful (a slow query, a model\nrun): the value stays <code>None</code> until Submit, then updates in one go. <strong>batch</strong>\nis for laying controls out inside a sentence of markdown rather than\nstacking them.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "AjVT",
      "code_hash": "719e7ff45cc2ee6f10564e8c1572f07b",
